WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.388
Microsoft's starting point is Learn's
page on listing role assignments.

2
00:00:04.388 --> 00:00:09.101
It covers the admin center, PowerShell
and Graph itself, and its all-roles

3
00:00:09.101 --> 00:00:14.363
sample reads every role definition, then
lists each role's assignments one by one.

4
00:00:14.363 --> 00:00:18.060
For Azure, Learn says there's no
single command for both kinds,

5
00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:21.388
so you list eligible and
active schedules separately.

6
00:00:21.388 --> 00:00:26.375
Those samples only live inside the web
page, so the repository pins the page's

7
00:00:26.375 --> 00:00:31.524
source unmodified, checks its hash in a
test, and watches for upstream changes.

8
00:00:31.524 --> 00:00:36.562
A harness then runs the samples,
exactly as published, against stand-ins.

9
00:00:36.562 --> 00:00:37.820
Nothing signs in.
